<headroom-library version="1" id="clean-glassy-single-coil" category="Clean" order="170" instrument="guitar" style="Pop / R&amp;B">
  <description>Glassy, hollow 'in-between pickup' quack: low-mids thinned and a presence peak lifted before a clean blackface twin, light compression and a short silver plate. Use positions 2 or 4 on a single-coil guitar for the real thing; fingerstyle snaps and R&amp;B double-stops pop right out.</description>
  <tags><tag>Clean</tag><tag>Pop / R&amp;B</tag><tag>Quack</tag><tag>Compressed</tag><tag>Plate Reverb</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://www.guitarplayer.com/players/mark-knopfler-down-the-road-wherever" title="Guitar Player: Mark Knopfler looks back (Twin + Strat, switch jammed between positions)"/>
    <source url="https://guitarearo.substack.com/p/mark-knopfler-sultans-strat-not-out-of-phase" title="Guitar Earo: the Sultans of Swing Strat was not out of phase"/>
    <source url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dire_Straits_(album)" title="Dire Straits (album) (Wikipedia)"/>
    <source url="https://www.musicradar.com/news/cory-wong-the-key-to-it-all-the-starting-point-for-understanding-is-just-to-listen" title="MusicRadar: Cory Wong interview (position 4, always-on compressor, records DI)"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
